jobs.description:
Role description

The Digital Engagement and Campaigns Officer is responsible for the  digital community of FYEG and for supporting the digital campaigning strategy of the organisation. This means managing FYEG's avenues of participation for digital sympathisers and volunteers and supporting the implementation of FYEG's digital campaigns and actions: (1) Dynamising and moderating the digital community of the organisation hosted on FYEG's internal digital platform, (2) Creation of digital fundraising campaigns on Lunda with the support of the Communication and Campaigns Officer, (3) Participating in the conceptualization and preparation of digital campaigns in cooperation the Communication and Campaigns Officer, (4) Acting as a bridge between the digital community and the Executive Committee, and vice-versa, (5) Managing FYEG's CRM system, (6) Coordinating and keeping contact with relevant stakeholders to create coordinated actions related to the campaigns. The Digital Engagement and Campaigns Officer will also support the general functioning and development of FYEG's activities with ad-hoc tasks.



This is a position requiring good organisation and time management skills, responsibility, ability to work independently and often with tight deadlines. The  Digital Engagement and Campaigns Officer works under the supervision of the Secretary-General of FYEG.

Requirements:

• Proven experience in copy writing;
• Experience in digital campaigning (petitions, mass mailing,...) and digital organising ;
• Very good computer skills and digital literacy (knowledge of Action Network or similar Customer Relations Management tools);
• Experience working with volunteers;
• Basic experience in online and in-person event planning;
• Good organisational and time management skills;
• Ability to take initiative and problem solving attitude;
• Proficiency in the English language, written and spoken;
• Good people skills and the ability to work in multi-cultural teams and environments;
• Good teamwork and personal communication skills;
• Flexibility to travel and occasionally work during evenings or weekend;
• Alignment with the goals and values of FYEG.

Additional assets:

• Previous involvement in a local or international youth organisation;
• Knowledge and experience with non-formal education methodology;
• Understanding of Green values such as ecology, feminism, anti-racism and social justice;
• Basic experience in fundraising, particularly small-donors fundraising;
• Knowledge of other languages;
• Experience working in the non-profit sector;
• Previous participation in FYEG events and bodies;
• Experience with Discord or similar digital platform.
Equal opportunity: 

FYEG strives to promote gender balance, diversity and inclusion within its structures. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment based on mutual respect and to promoting active political participation of persons with disabilities and of disadvantaged groups. All applicants are encouraged to submit their application and to self-identify if they wish to, on either their cover letter or CV. In case of equal appreciation on competence and suitability for the position, preference will be given to applicants from disadvantaged groups. In any case responses will remain confidential within the human resource responsibles.

Working conditions

Job Title: Digital Engagement and Campaigns Officer
Line Manager: Secretary General
Contract: Permanent Contract 
Working hours: 35 hours/week over 5 days with flexible working hours, core working hours between 10:00 and 16:00 and possible teleworking
Salary (gross): 2550€/month gross salary (approximately 2185€ net, depending on your personal situation)

Benefits:

• 8€ worth meal-vouchers for every day worked (averaging 160€/month)
• Coverage of daily transport between home and work (amount dependent on the distance and mode of transport)
• Telework allowance of 125€ per month 
Holidays:

• 20 days of paid legal holidays per year
• additional holidays between December 25th and 31st
Where:
The selected candidate will be required to be based in Belgium from the start of the contract in November (exact date negotiable)
